{"author":"Rebar Bot","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","author_sig":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","data":{"body":"Second plan review 2026-10-18 (BLOCK, 2 moves), both confirmed against origin/main b97d414b8e2 and fixed in the description:\n\n1. Wrong cite: the plan said `_NON_REPLAY_KNOWN_TYPES` is consumed by `fsck_scan.py:248`. It is not; `fsck_scan.py:244-250` builds the `ensures:`/`authorship:` summary lines and the file never names the set. The only external reader is `_engine_support/bridge_fsck.py:113,115` (the other hits are docstrings in `llm/completion_sidecar.py`, `llm/plan_review/sidecar.py`, `_store/event_prepare.py`, and the to-be-deleted `llm/overlap/digest_sidecar.py`). Approach now cites `bridge_fsck.py:115` alone.\n2. Dangling index link: `docs/README.md:142` links `calibration/overlap_batch_confidence.md`, which the plan deletes, and `scripts/check_docs_index.py --check` (gated by `tests/unit/test_check_docs_index.py`) fails on a missing target. Scope now deletes that README link alongside the two calibration files, and a new AC requires `git grep -n overlap_batch_confidence -- docs` to be empty and the docs-index check to exit 0.\n\nAlso added `docs/README.md` to file impact."},"env_id":"eea68b7f-6697-488b-ac52-744e2ed8e96f","event_type":"COMMENT","timestamp":1792365890063618990,"uuid":"07a719f0-4d30-4d4d-ae31-d602b0a1c766"}